\title{LCM}
\date{2026-04-16T22:16:42Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\taxon{Definition}
\p{The \em{least common multiple} of #{a, b \in \N}, written #{\lcm(a,b)}, is the unique natural number such that for all #{m \in \N}, ##{(\lcm(a,b) \mid m)
    \iff (a \mid m \land b \mid m).}}

\p{We won’t talk much more about #{\lcm}—it has very similar properties to #{\gcd} but with everything flipped.}

